mode: "100644"
text: "# Routing recipes + two worked briefs\n\n## \"I need X\" → route (verify-quarterly; pick by job, then current tool)\n- **B-roll for a Reel/Short (cinematic cutaway)** → generative: Veo 3.1 (all-round + native audio\n  → veo-3), Kling 3.0 (4K value → kling), Runway Gen-4.5 (tight camera control → runway). Keep clips short.\n- **Faceless talking-head explainer** → avatar: HeyGen (heygen — creator/social) or Synthesia\n  (synthesia — enterprise/L&D/localization). Add VO from ElevenLabs (ai-voiceover) only if not\n  using the avatar's own voice.\n- **Narration over slides/footage** → voiceover: ElevenLabs (ai-voiceover).\n- **Turn a long video into Shorts + sound-off captions** → clip+captions: Opus Clip / CapCut /\n  Submagic (captions-and-clipping). Powers youtube-shorts and the Shorts→long funnel.\n- **Atmospheric / nature / HDR mood shot** → Luma Ray3 (luma — silent; sound in post).\n- **Fast, cheap concept test before committing** → Pika / Hailuo / Luma drafts, then finalize on Veo/Kling.\n- **A real human on camera (founder/trust content)** → film it → talking-head-and-piece-to-camera.\n- **A real product or place you have** → don't generate it. **Film it** (see below).\n\n## The default that saves the most trust: film it instead\nGenerated footage of **real things you actually have** (your product, cafe, team) reads as fake and\nundercuts trust and originality signals. **Generate B-roll for what you can't film** (impossible,\nexpensive, abstract); **film the proof** for everything real. Generated clips stay as short cutaways.\nFor the on-camera human (founder POV, testimonials, trust pieces), the craft lives in\n**talking-head-and-piece-to-camera** — an avatar or generated stand-in is the wrong route.\n\n## Worked brief 1 — blunt indie-founder voice (generative B-roll for a Reel)\n```\nJOB: generative B-roll (cutaway, ~3s)\nSUBJECT/ACTION/SETTING: a single coin dropping into a clean glass jar; tidy kitchen counter\nLIGHT+MOOD/CAMERA/ASPECT/DURATION: soft morning light, calm; slow push-in; 9:16; 3s\nAUDIO: native SFX (coin clink) — Veo can do this in one pass\nBRAND: muted, tidy palette (brand-profile)\nROUTE: generative -> Veo 3.1 (native audio) | Kling 3.0 if cost matters -> veo-3 for the prompt\nDISCLOSURE: \"AI-generated B-roll\" in caption; YouTube Altered-Content if used on Shorts\nNOTE: the messy-spreadsheet shot is screen-recorded, not generated (real proof).\n```\n\n## Worked brief 2 — warm studio voice (faceless explainer)\n```\nJOB: avatar talking-head (~30s) + VO\nSUBJECT/ACTION/SETTING: friendly presenter, calm desk background, explaining the 30% tax rule\nLIGHT+MOOD/CAMERA/ASPECT/DURATION: warm, soft; static medium; 9:16; ~30s\nAUDIO: ElevenLabs VO (warm, unhurried) OR the avatar's built-in voice\nBRAND: soft palette, low-pressure tone (voice-builder)\nROUTE: avatar -> HeyGen (heygen) or Synthesia (synthesia) ; VO -> ElevenLabs (ai-voiceover)\nDISCLOSURE: on-screen \"Created with an AI presenter\"; TikTok auto-discloses; EU AI Act\nNOTE: consented/owned avatar only — never a real non-consenting person's likeness.\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + voice-builder first; portable brief (no vendor lock-in); generated clips\nare cutaways the human assembles; finished video → scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial; AI disclosed.\nConsumers of these briefs: reels-script (veo-prompt-pack), tiktok-script, youtube-shorts,\nyoutube-long-form, cross-platform-repurposing.\n"
